  "body": "Sometimes, slottables already have IDs, so it's not necessary to require them to also define reduntant `slot` attributes. If a `slot` is able to find its slottables by slottables's IDs, we would go a step further to make the document semantically brief(_It's semantical brevity_ which is one principial cause that inspires shadow DOM, isn't it?).\r\n\r\nI'd like suggest we add a `for` attribute to <slot> for this.\r\n\r\n```\r\n<slot for=\"id-for-the-slottable\"></slot>\r\n```",
